{"id":1330,"date":"2020-11-26T18:17:07","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T02:17:07","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1330"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:48","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:48","slug":"sumo-competition-rules","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/sumo-competition-rules\/","title":{"rendered":"Sumo Competition Rules"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221611818a9\" name=\"6a221611818a9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The field<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The field is a 48&#8243; x 48&#8243; white surface. Inside is a circle with a 40&#8243; diameter bordered by black eletrical tape. The tape is 0.75&#8243; thick. Yours should look similar to the picture below:[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1331&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221611819ea\" name=\"6a221611819ea\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Rules and regulations<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Robots should be built with the Smart Inventor Board.<\/li>\n<li>The size limit for your Sumo Bot is 8.5\u2033 x 8.5\u2033, width by length. Your robot cannot go outside of that size limit\u00a0<em>at any time<\/em>\u00a0during the match!<\/li>\n<li>There is no height limit (woohoo!).<\/li>\n<li>Only two motors may be used on the robot.<\/li>\n<li>The robot must be autonomous<em>\u00a0&#8212;\u00a0<\/em>it should not be remote controlled.<\/li>\n<li>The robot cannot exceed 1.5 pounds in weight.<\/li>\n<li>The robot must buzz within the first five seconds to indicate that it is about to start.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 3 The field [vc_column_text]The field is a 48\" x 48\" white surface. Inside is a circle with a 40\" diameter bordered by black eletrical tape. The tape is&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/sumo-competition-rules\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1733,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2163,2215,2171,2187,2188],"class_list":["post-1330","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-competition-rules","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-sumo","lesson-tag-sumo-bot","module-sumo","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1330","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1330\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1332,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1330\/revisions\/1332"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1733"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1330"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1330"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post